    <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>Last updated: January 2026</p></div></section>
    <section class="legal-content"><div class="container"><div class="legal-body">
        <h2>1. Data Collection</h2><p>TinyBin does <strong>not</strong> collect, store, or transmit any personal data. All your projects, code, and settings are stored locally in your browser using the Web Storage API (LocalStorage). Nothing is sent to our servers.</p>
        <h2>2. GitHub API</h2><p>When you paste a GitHub repository URL, TinyBin makes requests to the GitHub public API to fetch repository metadata and file contents. These requests are made directly from your browser to GitHub's servers. We do not proxy or log these requests.</p>
        <h2>3. Web Serial API</h2><p>When you flash firmware to a microcontroller, TinyBin uses the Web Serial API to communicate directly with your device via USB. This communication happens entirely within your browser and device — no data passes through our servers.</p>
        <h2>4. Cookies</h2><p>TinyBin does not use tracking cookies, analytics cookies, or advertising cookies. We may use essential browser storage for IDE functionality only.</p>
        <h2>5. Third-Party Services</h2><p>TinyBin loads resources from the following third-party CDNs: <strong>Google Fonts</strong> for typography and <strong>Cloudflare CDN</strong> for Ace Editor library. These services may collect standard CDN access logs as per their own privacy policies.</p>
        <h2>6. Changes</h2><p>We may update this privacy policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated revision date.</p>
        <h2>7. Contact</h2><p>If you have questions about this privacy policy, contact us at <a href="mailto:privacy@tinybin.dev">privacy@tinybin.dev</a>.</p>
    </div></div></section>
